cf0fe435db4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130954" :question/id #uuid "02830b84-264a-5296-8703-bbcf95ce7d55" :question/math-academy-id "q-130954" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $P$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 7 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $P$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 7 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $1$st column." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130954/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130954"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
